          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪ್ರಸಾರ — prasāra — \"a broadcast; spreading\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಆ ಪಂದ್ಯದ ಪ್ರಸಾರ ಸಂಜೆ ಆರು ಗಂಟೆಗೆ ಶುರುವಾಯಿತು. ā pandyada prasāra sañje āru gaṇṭege śuruvāyitu. The broadcast of that match began at six in the evening."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Radio and television both have a ಪ್ರಸಾರ (prasāra). ಪ್ರಸಾರವಾಗು means to be broadcast."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪ್ರಸಾರ (prasāra) is borrowed from Sanskrit prasāra, \"spreading out, extension\" (CDIAL 8835). A broadcast spreads a programme far and wide."
            }
          ]
        },
